sparse trigram separation: worst TRUE -2.8689  vs  best WRONG -4.7134
  margin +1.8445  (separates)

dense / sparse equivalence on hole-free geometry (arm A):
  dense  GermanTrigrams.score(plaintext) : -2.847037
  sparse meanLogProbability(order 3)     : -2.847037
  |delta| 0.00e+00  →  IDENTICAL statistic
  dense IC 0.063866 vs sparse IC 0.063866

threshold transfer:
  dense break bar        : -3.600
  dense German reference : -2.847
  dense noise reference  : -5.382
  sparse TRUE            : -2.8470 exact / -2.8689 post-gap
  sparse WRONG (best)    : -4.7134
  Same statistic and same units, so the -3.600 bar is comparable in SCALE.
  Two caveats that are not scale problems:
   * the dense `tailScore` excises crib positions and concatenates, inventing
     adjacency the sparse path refuses — a sparse tail is a different SAMPLE;
   * fewer eligible windows means a noisier estimate, so a barrier-heavy
     candidate deserves less confidence at the same mean.

*** SPARSE CALIBRATION PASS ***
The sparse path reproduces the control plaintext on both geometries, keeps the
hole as a scoring barrier, separates the true key, and reproduces the dense
trigram statistic exactly on hole-free geometry. It is fit to adjudicate
exact/no-drop post-gap candidates against the existing bar, with window count
reported alongside every score. It sets no bar for REPAIRED candidates:
crib-exactness is undefined for them by construction.
